\tag{status}
\meta{updated}{2026-11-24}
\meta{pr}{17}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Rewritten on 2026-11-24 in session [ses-YOB8](ses-YOB8); the earlier text described hypotheses and certificate sets that no longer exist ([dec-US4Q](dec-US4Q)).}

\p{\strong{The proof is not complete.} \code{\verb~|expf_correctlyRounded~} in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Extracted/Expf/Main.lean~} states that \code{\verb~|math::double_eval::expf~}, extracted from LLVM libc at \code{\verb~|e1a5f92db023~}, is correctly rounded in the four rounding directions of C and reaches no operation that C++ leaves undefined. Its proof uses two lemmas that end in \code{\verb~|sorry~}.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Inputs}\th{Bit patterns}\th{Share}\th{State}}
\tr{\td{Zeros, infinities, NaNs, magnitude at most 2⁻²⁶, overflow, underflow}\td{3 749 616 693}\td{87.30 \%}\td{proved, \code{\verb~|Paths/Ranges.lean~}}}
\tr{\td{2⁻²⁶ < x < 88.72…}\td{271 675 927}\td{6.33 \%}\td{open, \code{\verb~|Expf.correctAt_main_pos~}}}
\tr{\td{-103.97… < x < -2⁻²⁶}\td{273 674 676}\td{6.37 \%}\td{open, \code{\verb~|Expf.correctAt_main_neg~}}}
}

\p{\strong{How the open part is to be proved.} By numerical analysis of the computation with the tables and the polynomial: [prob-48KJ](prob-48KJ). One step is done, the distance of the polynomial from the exponential ([log-7DAL](log-7DAL)).}

\p{\strong{What the statement rests on.} The translation by \code{\verb~|ast2lean~} and the definitions of \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Core/~}, which are tested against the compiled code and not proved; FloatLib's model of IEEE 754 arithmetic. \code{\verb~|errno~} and the exception flags are outside the statement: [prob-VR5Z](prob-VR5Z).}

\p{\strong{Other plans.} \code{\verb~|double_eval_fma~}, \code{\verb~|integer_eval~}, \code{\verb~|static_rounding~}, \code{\verb~|float_eval~} and \code{\verb~|float_eval_cr_rn~} are extracted and tested. Nothing is stated or proved about them.}
